{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Thus shall you say to the house of Jacob.</b> These are the women. 'Thus shall you say' — in the holy tongue; 'thus shall you say' — gently. And He commanded to speak to the women first, to teach them discipline and proper conduct, and further so as to draw the heart of the child toward Torah and commandments, and to say to them only chapter headings, because their mind is not as settled as that of men. And further, the good woman is a cause for Torah, for she can draw her son to the study hall because she is constantly at home, and she takes pity on him with all kinds of enticements in order to draw him to the study of Torah from his youth, so that even when he grows old he will not depart from it. Therefore the woman is worthy to pray to HaShem, may He be blessed, at the time of kindling the Sabbath lamp — which is a commandment incumbent upon her — that HaShem grant her children illumined by Torah, for prayer is more readily heard at the time of performing a commandment, and in the merit of the Sabbath lamp, which is light, she merits children possessors of Torah, which is called light, as stated (Proverbs 6:23): ״כי נר מצוה ותורה אור״; and so the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: 'This one who is accustomed to lamps — he will have sons who are Torah scholars.'" "<b>And you shall tell the children of Israel.</b> He commanded to make known to them warnings and punishments, and this is the sense of ותגיד — telling things as hard as sinews (גידין), and therefore it is written full with a yod. And in all of Scripture you will not find the word הגדה except defective (חסר), such as (Joshua 7:19): ״והגד נא לי מה עשית״, (Isaiah 58:1): ״והגד לעמי פשעם״; but this one, which is written with a yod — therefore they expounded of it things as hard as sinews."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :register {:fixes 1}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:58.134609719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}